.el .ds Aq '
.TH orbit-import-todoist 1  "todoist " 
.SH NAME
orbit\-import\-todoist \- Import active Todoist items. The token is read from ORBIT_TODOIST_TOKEN or stdin, used once and never stored. Without \-\-yes it only previews the mapping
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit import todoist\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-map\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import active Todoist items. The token is read from ORBIT_TODOIST_TOKEN or stdin, used once and never stored. Without \-\-yes it only previews the mapping
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object per result, with `"v":1`, instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-map\fR \fI<MAPS>\fR
Change where a Todoist project goes: ID=area:NAME, ID=project:AREA/NAME or ID=inbox
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI colors
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Import for real
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  orbit import todoist
  orbit import todoist \-\-map 2201=project:Home/Garden
  orbit import todoist \-\-map 2201=inbox \-\-yes
